; 64-bit atomics whose old value is read back.
;
; `kernels/spirv/atomic.spvasm` covers the case where nobody reads the pair: an
; order-free operation whose result is dropped is a reduction, and a reduction is
; two 32-bit atomics. Here every old value is used, so the pair has to be read,
; changed and written back as one value — which this host builds out of a lock
; over the two halves, taken in lane order.
;
; The checks are arithmetic rather than a reference implementation, because the
; old values of an atomic are order-free as a set:
;
;   b0 += 1, summing the olds    the olds are a permutation of 0..n-1, so their
;                               sum is n(n-1)/2 exactly. A lost or duplicated
;                               update moves that number.
;   b2 = max(b2, 1), summing     the counter starts at 0 and 1 is the only value
;     the olds                 ever offered, so exactly one thread sees 0 and the
;                               rest see 1: the final counter is 1 and the olds
;                               sum to n-1. This is the 64-bit compare.
;   b4 = min(b4, -1), summing    the signed form, and the one that tells signed
;     the olds                 ordering from unsigned: signed, the counter ends at
;                               -1 and the olds sum to -(n-1) after one thread
;                               sees 0; read as unsigned, -1 is the largest value
;                               there is, so both stay 0.
;
; The sums go through `OpAtomicIAdd` with the result unused, which is the
; reduction that already existed at 64 bits — so this fixture exercises the new
; path and the old one in the same kernel.
               OpCapability Kernel
               OpCapability Addresses
               OpCapability Int64
               OpCapability Int64Atomics
               OpMemoryModel Physical64 OpenCL
               OpEntryPoint Kernel %main "atom64k"
               OpName %main "atom64k"
      %void = OpTypeVoid
       %u32 = OpTypeInt 32 0
       %u64 = OpTypeInt 64 0
       %i64 = OpTypeInt 64 1
      %u64p = OpTypePointer CrossWorkgroup %u64
      %i64p = OpTypePointer CrossWorkgroup %i64
      %fnty = OpTypeFunction %void %u64p %u64p %u64p %u64p %i64p %i64p
      %scp = OpConstant %u32 1
      %sem = OpConstant %u32 0
      %one = OpConstant %u64 1
      %cm1 = OpConstant %i64 -1
      %main = OpFunction %void None %fnty
        %a0 = OpFunctionParameter %u64p
        %a1 = OpFunctionParameter %u64p
        %a2 = OpFunctionParameter %u64p
        %a3 = OpFunctionParameter %u64p
        %a4 = OpFunctionParameter %i64p
        %a5 = OpFunctionParameter %i64p
     %entry = OpLabel
      %old0 = OpAtomicIAdd %u64 %a0 %scp %sem %one
     %keep0 = OpAtomicIAdd %u64 %a1 %scp %sem %old0
      %old2 = OpAtomicUMax %u64 %a2 %scp %sem %one
     %keep2 = OpAtomicIAdd %u64 %a3 %scp %sem %old2
      %old4 = OpAtomicSMin %i64 %a4 %scp %sem %cm1
     %keep4 = OpAtomicIAdd %i64 %a5 %scp %sem %old4
                OpReturn
                OpFunctionEnd
